Phase 4: Scripting & Assertions

- Script execution engine with sandboxed JS runner (new Function)
- Postman-compatible pm.test() and pm.expect() assertion API
- 15 matchers: toBe, toEqual, toBeDefined, toBeUndefined, toBeNull,
  toBeTruthy, toBeFalsy, toContain, toHaveLength, toBeLessThan,
  toBeGreaterThan, toMatch, toHaveProperty, toBeType, plus .not negation
- pm.response: code, json(), text(), headers.get/has, responseTime/Size
- pm.environment: get/set/unset/toObject for variable management
- Console capture: log, info, warn, error with timestamps
- Lightweight JSON Schema validator (type, required, properties, items,
  enum, min/max Length, min/max for numbers)
- Pre-request scripts: run before API call, can set variables
- Post-request test scripts: run after response, assert on results
- ScriptEditor component with line numbers, tab key support, and
  snippet insertion (8 test snippets + 4 pre-request snippets)
- TestResultsPanel: pass/fail icons, summary bar, error display
- ConsolePanel: color-coded log levels, timestamp, clear button
- ResponseViewer: added Tests and Console tabs alongside Body/Headers
- SingleRequest: added Pre-request and Tests panels, wired execution
  flow (pre-script → request → test script → display results)
- RequestTab type extended: preRequestScript, testScript fields
- TabResponse extended: testResults, consoleLogs, scriptError fields
- 66 new script engine tests, 136 frontend total, 172 backend (all pass)
